\paragraph{Contributions.}
Our work differs from concurrent studies in three respects:
\begin{enumerate}[nosep]
\item \textbf{Entity-level diagnostic decomposition.}
Where \citet{yao2026consistency} report task-level correlation ($\rho$ up to 0.47) and \citet{yun2025price} describe diversity collapse qualitatively, we decompose failures at instance level into degeneracy ($D$), oracle headroom ($G_{\textup{nd}}$), and signal alignment ($\alpha$), identifying $\alpha{\to}0$ as the binding constraint ($8$--$33{\times}$ tighter than degeneracy).
\item \textbf{Prescriptive entity construction.}
We formalize entity-level construction as MBR decoding (Proposition~\ref{prop:construction_mbr}) and identify conditions under which it yields gains ($+1.40$\,pp on Few-NERD; per-family Holm $p_{\text{adj}}{=}0.006$) versus inverse scaling (69\% of $N$-transitions).
\item \textbf{Mechanistic evidence.}
Hidden-state probes (AUROC $0.63$--$0.88$) reveal an introspection boundary: models encode entity quality internally but cannot access it through generation, explaining why prompt-based self-judgment fails (ESJ AUROC $0.51$).
\end{enumerate}

